1
00:00:30,363 --> 00:00:32,991
Read the charges.

2
00:00:33,074 --> 00:00:35,702
Dr. Jumba Jookiba--

3
00:00:35,744 --> 00:00:37,996
lead scientist of
Galaxy Defense Industries--

4
00:00:38,121 --> 00:00:41,583
you stand before this council

5
00:00:41,624 --> 00:00:46,004
accused of illegal
genetic experimentation.

6
00:00:52,010 --> 00:00:54,346
How do you plead?

7
00:00:54,387 --> 00:00:56,181
Not guilty!

8
00:00:56,222 --> 00:00:59,017
My experiments
are only theoretical--

9
00:00:59,059 --> 00:01:01,978
completely
within legal boundaries.

10
00:01:01,978 --> 00:01:06,524
We believe you actually
created something.

11
00:01:06,566 --> 00:01:09,361
Created something?! Ha!

12
00:01:09,402 --> 00:01:12,447
But that would be irresponsible
and unethical.

13
00:01:12,489 --> 00:01:14,199
I would never, ever...

14
00:01:15,909 --> 00:01:18,203
...make more than one.

15
00:01:25,418 --> 00:01:28,129
What is that monstrosity?

16
00:01:28,171 --> 00:01:29,381
Monstrosity!

17
00:01:29,422 --> 00:01:34,761
What you see before you
is the first of a new species.

18
00:01:34,803 --> 00:01:38,807
I call it Experiment 6-2-6.

19
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:42,852
He is bulletproof, fireproof

20
00:01:42,894 --> 00:01:45,689
and can think faster
than supercomputer.

21
00:01:45,730 --> 00:01:47,315
He can see in the dark

22
00:01:47,357 --> 00:01:49,984
and move objects
3,000 times his size.

23
00:01:50,026 --> 00:01:52,320
His only instinct:

24
00:01:52,362 --> 00:01:55,782
To destroy
everything he touches!

25
00:01:57,575 --> 00:01:59,285
So, it is a monster.

26
00:01:59,327 --> 00:02:00,745
Hey, just a little one.

27
00:02:00,787 --> 00:02:02,372
It is an affront to nature.

28
00:02:02,414 --> 00:02:04,082
It must be destroyed!

29
00:02:04,124 --> 00:02:06,042
Calm yourself, Captain Gantu.

30
00:02:06,084 --> 00:02:08,545
Perhaps it can be reasoned with.

31
00:02:08,586 --> 00:02:11,548
Experiment 6-2-6

32
00:02:11,589 --> 00:02:15,093
give us some sign you understand
any of this.

33
00:02:15,135 --> 00:02:19,723
Show us that there is something
inside you that is good.

34
00:02:22,726 --> 00:02:24,185
Hmm?

35
00:02:24,227 --> 00:02:26,688
Meega, nala kweesta!

36
00:02:29,315 --> 00:02:31,109
So naughty!

37
00:02:33,486 --> 00:02:35,155
I didn't teach it that.

38
00:02:35,196 --> 00:02:37,699
Place that idiot scientist
under arrest!

39
00:02:37,741 --> 00:02:42,787
I prefer to be called
"evil genius"!

40
00:02:42,829 --> 00:02:45,206
And as for that abomination...

41
00:02:46,416 --> 00:02:48,793
...it is the flawed product
of a deranged mind.

42
00:02:50,003 --> 00:02:51,379
It has no place among us.

43
00:02:51,421 --> 00:02:54,382
Captain Gantu, take him away.

44
00:02:54,424 --> 00:02:55,884
With pleasure.

45
00:03:10,273 --> 00:03:11,566
Hmm.

46
00:03:18,156 --> 00:03:19,115
Uncomfortable?

47
00:03:19,157 --> 00:03:20,116
Oh...

48
00:03:20,158 --> 00:03:21,409
Good!

49
00:03:21,451 --> 00:03:25,789
The council has banished you
to exile on a desert asteroid.

50
00:03:25,830 --> 00:03:28,792
So, relax... enjoy the trip

51
00:03:28,833 --> 00:03:30,794
and don't get any ideas.

52
00:03:30,835 --> 00:03:34,839
These guns are locked
onto your genetic signature.

53
00:03:34,881 --> 00:03:36,675
They won't shoot anyone but you.

54
00:03:37,884 --> 00:03:38,968
Ow! Why, you...!

55
00:03:40,679 --> 00:03:43,848
May I remind the captain
that he is on duty.

56
00:03:45,558 --> 00:03:47,102
Secure the cell!

57
00:03:47,143 --> 00:03:48,978
Aye, Captain.

58
00:03:52,565 --> 00:03:54,859
Captain on deck.

59
00:03:54,901 --> 00:03:56,945
All ahead full.

60
00:04:00,407 --> 00:04:04,494
Do... Does this, uh,
look infected to you?

61
00:04:21,928 --> 00:04:24,723
Oh!

62
00:04:32,939 --> 00:04:34,315
Quiet, you.

63
00:04:38,236 --> 00:04:39,487
Gunfire in the cell bay!

64
00:04:39,529 --> 00:04:40,530
Open a channel.

65
00:04:51,082 --> 00:04:52,000
He's loose on Deck C!

66
00:04:52,083 --> 00:04:53,543
Red alert.
Seal off the deck!

67
00:05:01,926 --> 00:05:03,762
Security,
converge on door seven!

68
00:05:03,803 --> 00:05:06,014
Deadly force authorized.

69
00:05:06,056 --> 00:05:07,849
Fire on sight!

70
00:05:07,891 --> 00:05:09,517
There he is!

71
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:15,732
Security to Bridge.

72
00:05:15,774 --> 00:05:17,400
It's in the ventilation system.

73
00:05:19,986 --> 00:05:22,072
He's headed for the power...

74
00:05:23,114 --> 00:05:24,074
...grid.

75
00:05:26,451 --> 00:05:28,536
What was that?

76
00:05:28,578 --> 00:05:31,122
I don't think he's
on the ship anymore.

77
00:05:31,164 --> 00:05:33,875
Confirmed.
He's taken a police cruiser.

78
00:05:35,710 --> 00:05:38,129
Yeah... he took the red one.

79
00:05:39,714 --> 00:05:40,840
Yee-haw!

80
00:05:58,191 --> 00:05:59,401
Hmm?!

81
00:05:59,442 --> 00:06:00,819
That's it!

82
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:02,737
We got it.
We got it!

83
00:06:05,949 --> 00:06:07,909
Hyperdrive activated.

84
00:06:08,034 --> 00:06:08,952
System charging.

85
00:06:09,035 --> 00:06:10,954
He's engaged his H-drive!

86
00:06:10,995 --> 00:06:13,498
Warning--
guidance is not functional.

87
00:06:13,540 --> 00:06:14,499
Pursuit Commander

88
00:06:14,541 --> 00:06:16,626
that crazy trog is
about to make a jump!

89
00:06:16,668 --> 00:06:19,212
Break formation!
Get clear of that ship!

90
00:06:19,254 --> 00:06:20,880
Navigation failure.

91
00:06:20,922 --> 00:06:23,383
Do not engage hyper...

92
00:06:31,975 --> 00:06:35,103
Get me Galactic Control.

93
00:06:36,312 --> 00:06:37,939
Where is he?!

94
00:06:37,981 --> 00:06:39,357
He's still in hyperspace.

95
00:06:39,399 --> 00:06:40,817
Where will he exit?

96
00:06:40,859 --> 00:06:41,943
Calculating now--

97
00:06:42,027 --> 00:06:46,197
quadrant 17, section 0-0-5,
area 51.

98
00:06:46,239 --> 00:06:49,242
A planet called... Ee-arth.

99
00:06:49,284 --> 00:06:51,953
I want an expert on this planet
in here now!

100
00:06:53,163 --> 00:06:54,706
What is that?

101
00:06:54,748 --> 00:06:56,833
Water. Most of the planet
is covered in it.

102
00:06:56,875 --> 00:06:58,335
He won't survive in water.

103
00:06:58,376 --> 00:07:00,378
His molecular density
is too great.

104
00:07:05,050 --> 00:07:07,010
No...

105
00:07:11,723 --> 00:07:13,850
Of course.

106
00:07:13,892 --> 00:07:15,518
How much time do we have?

107
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:19,064
We have projected his landing
at three hours, 42 minutes.

108
00:07:19,105 --> 00:07:20,607
Oh, we have to gas the planet.

109
00:07:20,648 --> 00:07:22,025
Hold it!

110
00:07:22,067 --> 00:07:23,151
Hold everything!

111
00:07:23,193 --> 00:07:25,945
Earth is a protected
wildlife preserve.

112
00:07:25,987 --> 00:07:27,655
Yeah. We've been using it

113
00:07:27,697 --> 00:07:30,033
to rebuild
the mosquito population

114
00:07:30,075 --> 00:07:33,661
which, need I remind you,
is an endangered species!

115
00:07:33,703 --> 00:07:36,539
Am I to assume
you are the expert?

116
00:07:36,581 --> 00:07:40,335
Oh, I don't know about "expert."

117
00:07:41,378 --> 00:07:42,962
Agent Pleakley at your service.

118
00:07:43,046 --> 00:07:44,798
Can we not simply
destroy the island?

119
00:07:44,839 --> 00:07:46,716
No! Crazyhead!

120
00:07:46,716 --> 00:07:49,719
The mosquito's food of choice,
primitive humanoid life forms

121
00:07:49,719 --> 00:07:51,471
have colonies
all over that planet.

122
00:07:51,513 --> 00:07:53,765
Are they intelligent?

123
00:07:53,807 --> 00:07:55,392
No, but they're very delicate.

124
00:07:55,433 --> 00:07:58,269
In fact, every time an asteroid
strikes their planet

125
00:07:58,311 --> 00:08:00,689
they have to begin life
all over.

126
00:08:01,815 --> 00:08:03,108
It's fascinating, isn't it?

127
00:08:03,149 --> 00:08:05,026
With this,
I've been able to study...

128
00:08:05,068 --> 00:08:07,362
What if our military forces
just landed there?

129
00:08:07,404 --> 00:08:09,030
Well, that'd be a bad idea!

130
00:08:09,072 --> 00:08:11,574
These are extremely
simple creatures, miss.

131
00:08:11,616 --> 00:08:15,245
Landing there would create mass
mayhem and planet-wide panic!

132
00:08:15,286 --> 00:08:18,164
A quiet capture would require
an understanding of 6-2-6

133
00:08:18,206 --> 00:08:19,416
that we do not possess!

134
00:08:19,457 --> 00:08:24,713
Who, then, Mr. Pleakley, would
you send for his extraction?

135
00:08:24,754 --> 00:08:27,424
Does he have a brother?

136
00:08:28,466 --> 00:08:30,427
Close grandmother, perhaps?

137
00:08:33,722 --> 00:08:35,348
Friendly cousin?

138
00:08:35,390 --> 00:08:37,767
Neighbor with a beard?

139
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:01,291
He got away?

140
00:09:01,332 --> 00:09:03,918
I'm sure this comes
as no surprise to you.

141
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:07,339
I designed this creature
for to be unstoppable.

142
00:09:07,380 --> 00:09:10,592
Which is precisely why you
must now bring him back.

143
00:09:10,633 --> 00:09:11,760
What? Me?

144
00:09:11,801 --> 00:09:13,345
And to reward you

145
00:09:13,386 --> 00:09:18,433
we are willing to trade
your freedom for his capture.

146
00:09:19,684 --> 00:09:22,645
6-2-6 will not come easily.

147
00:09:22,687 --> 00:09:25,315
Maybe direct hit
from plasma cannon

148
00:09:25,357 --> 00:09:27,859
might stun him long enough to...

149
00:09:27,901 --> 00:09:28,943
Plasma cannon granted.

150
00:09:29,027 --> 00:09:31,821
Do we have a bargain, Dr. Jumba?

151
00:09:33,156 --> 00:09:34,741
B-B-But it's a delicate planet!

152
00:09:34,783 --> 00:09:36,868
Who's going to control him?

153
00:09:36,910 --> 00:09:38,870
You will.

154
00:09:38,912 --> 00:09:40,413
Very good, Your Highness.

155
00:09:40,455 --> 00:09:41,539
I... I didn't quite...

156
00:09:42,749 --> 00:09:43,875
Uh, you're notjoking!

157
00:09:43,917 --> 00:09:48,129
So, tell me,
my little one-eyed one

158
00:09:48,171 --> 00:09:53,134
on what poor, pitiful,
defenseless planet

159
00:09:53,343 --> 00:09:59,557
has my monstrosity
been unleashed?

160
00:09:59,599 --> 00:10:01,559
# Mahalo nui ia #

161
00:10:01,601 --> 00:10:03,561
# Ke Ali iwahine #

162
00:10:03,603 --> 00:10:05,563
# O Lili ulani #

163
00:10:05,605 --> 00:10:08,942
# O ka Wohi ku #

164
00:10:08,983 --> 00:10:12,779
# Ka pipio mai o ke anuenue #

165
00:10:12,821 --> 00:10:18,618
# Na waihooluu a halikeole #

166
00:10:18,660 --> 00:10:23,289
# E nana na maka
i ke ao malama #

167
00:10:23,331 --> 00:10:30,130
# Mai Hawaii akea i Kauai... #

168
00:10:36,678 --> 00:10:39,973
# O Kal'kaua he inoa #

169
00:10:40,015 --> 00:10:44,102
# O Ka pua mae ole i ka I' #

170
00:10:44,144 --> 00:10:47,355
# Ka pua maila i ka mauna #

171
00:10:47,397 --> 00:10:51,359
# I ke kuahiwi o Mauna Kea #

172
00:10:51,401 --> 00:10:55,363
# Ke 'maila i K'lauea #

173
00:10:55,405 --> 00:10:59,492
# M'lamalama i Wahinekapu #

174
00:10:59,534 --> 00:11:02,954
# A ka luna o Uw'kahuna #

175
00:11:02,996 --> 00:11:06,791
# I ka pali kapu o Ka auea #

176
00:11:06,833 --> 00:11:10,545
# Ea mai ke ali i kia manu #

177
00:11:10,587 --> 00:11:14,632
# Ua wehi i ka hulu o ka mamo #

178
00:11:14,674 --> 00:11:17,844
# Ka pua nani a o Hawai i #

179
00:11:17,886 --> 00:11:23,058
# O Kal'kaua he inoa #

180
00:11:26,061 --> 00:11:28,980
# O Kal'kaua he inoa #

181
00:11:29,064 --> 00:11:33,526
# Ka pua mae ole i ka I' #

182
00:11:33,568 --> 00:11:36,363
# Ka pua maila i ka mauna #

183
00:11:36,404 --> 00:11:38,365
# I ke kuahiwi o Mauna Kea #

184
00:11:40,867 --> 00:11:43,286
# Ke 'maila i K'lauea... #

185
00:11:43,328 --> 00:11:45,163
One, two, three, four...

186
00:11:45,205 --> 00:11:47,165
# ...M'lamalama i
Wahinekapu... #

187
00:11:47,207 --> 00:11:48,833
Ay-yi-yi.

188
00:11:48,875 --> 00:11:52,003
# ...A ka luna o Uw'kahuna #

189
00:11:52,128 --> 00:11:56,174
# I ka pali kapu o Ka auea #

190
00:11:56,216 --> 00:11:58,009
# Mahalo nui ia #

191
00:11:58,134 --> 00:12:00,428
# Ke Ali iwahine #

192
00:12:00,470 --> 00:12:01,930
# O Lili ulani #

193
00:12:02,055 --> 00:12:05,350
# O ka Wohi ku... #

194
00:12:05,392 --> 00:12:08,812
# Ea mai ke ali i kia manu #

195
00:12:08,812 --> 00:12:13,358
# Ua wehi i ka hulu o ka mamo #

196
00:12:13,400 --> 00:12:16,361
# Ka pua nani a o Hawai I #

197
00:12:16,403 --> 00:12:20,323
# O Kal'kaua he inoa... #

198
00:12:20,323 --> 00:12:24,411
He Inoa No Kalani Kalakaua
Kulele.

199
00:12:24,452 --> 00:12:25,412
-Whoa!
-Whoa!

200
00:12:26,788 --> 00:12:28,373
Stop. Stop.

201
00:12:28,415 --> 00:12:32,252
Lilo, why are you all wet?

202
00:12:32,293 --> 00:12:34,087
It's sandwich day.

203
00:12:36,798 --> 00:12:38,967
Every Thursday,
I take Pudge the fish

204
00:12:39,009 --> 00:12:40,510
a peanut butter sandwich.

205
00:12:40,552 --> 00:12:42,095
Pudge is a fish?

206
00:12:42,137 --> 00:12:44,973
And today we were out
of peanut butter!

207
00:12:45,015 --> 00:12:47,642
So I asked my sister
what to give him

208
00:12:47,684 --> 00:12:49,853
and she said a tuna sandwich.

209
00:12:49,894 --> 00:12:51,646
I can't give Pudge tuna!

210
00:12:51,688 --> 00:12:54,607
Do you know what tuna is?

211
00:12:54,649 --> 00:12:55,650
Fish?

212
00:12:55,692 --> 00:12:57,318
It's fish!

213
00:12:57,360 --> 00:13:01,156
If I gave Pudge tuna,
I'd be an abomination!

214
00:13:01,197 --> 00:13:03,575
I'm late because
I had to go to the store

215
00:13:03,616 --> 00:13:04,868
and get peanut butter

216
00:13:04,909 --> 00:13:07,245
'cause all we have
is-is stinkin' tuna!

217
00:13:07,287 --> 00:13:10,623
Lilo, Lilo, why is
this so important?

218
00:13:10,665 --> 00:13:12,709
Pudge controls the weather.

219
00:13:15,378 --> 00:13:16,880
You're crazy.

220
00:13:20,091 --> 00:13:21,176
Please! Please!

221
00:13:21,217 --> 00:13:23,261
Everybody calm down!

222
00:13:24,471 --> 00:13:25,597
Girls...

223
00:13:27,140 --> 00:13:28,475
Shh.

224
00:13:28,516 --> 00:13:29,726
Lilo...

225
00:13:29,768 --> 00:13:30,935
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

226
00:13:30,977 --> 00:13:32,562
I won't do it again!

227
00:13:32,604 --> 00:13:34,856
Maybe we should call
your sister.

228
00:13:34,898 --> 00:13:36,316
No! I'll be good!

229
00:13:36,358 --> 00:13:37,650
I want to dance.

230
00:13:37,692 --> 00:13:40,111
I practiced.

231
00:13:40,153 --> 00:13:41,821
I just want to dance.

232
00:13:41,863 --> 00:13:45,784
I practiced.

233
00:13:45,825 --> 00:13:47,827
Ooh, she bit me.

234
00:13:47,869 --> 00:13:49,704
Eww!

235
00:13:56,044 --> 00:13:57,754
I called your sister.

236
00:13:57,796 --> 00:14:01,383
She said to wait for her
here on the porch.

237
00:14:01,424 --> 00:14:04,302
We'll try again on Sunday.

238
00:14:11,142 --> 00:14:13,311
Does this look infected
to you?

239
00:14:13,353 --> 00:14:14,479
Yeah.

240
00:14:15,689 --> 00:14:17,148
You better not have rabies.

241
00:14:17,190 --> 00:14:18,316
If you have rabies

242
00:14:18,358 --> 00:14:20,777
the dogcatcher is
going to have to cut...

243
00:14:20,819 --> 00:14:22,862
Are you going to play dolls?

244
00:14:22,904 --> 00:14:25,448
You don't have a doll.

245
00:14:25,490 --> 00:14:27,784
This is Scrump.

246
00:14:29,035 --> 00:14:31,121
I made her,
but her head is too big.

247
00:14:31,162 --> 00:14:34,791
So I pretend a bug laid eggs
in her ears, and she's upset

248
00:14:34,833 --> 00:14:37,502
because she only has
a few more days to...

249
00:14:56,646 --> 00:14:58,565
Lilo!

250
00:14:58,606 --> 00:15:00,692
Lilo?

251
00:15:04,154 --> 00:15:07,157
Lilo?

252
00:15:07,198 --> 00:15:09,117
Oh, no.

253
00:15:10,702 --> 00:15:12,495
You better be home.

254
00:15:17,334 --> 00:15:19,210
Hey! Watch where you're going!

255
00:15:19,252 --> 00:15:20,545
Stupidhead!

256
00:15:25,884 --> 00:15:28,553
# I found a new place
to dwell... #

257
00:15:28,595 --> 00:15:30,972
Oh, Lilo!

258
00:15:31,056 --> 00:15:33,183
Lilo! Open the door, Lilo!

259
00:15:33,224 --> 00:15:34,893
Go away.

260
00:15:34,934 --> 00:15:36,728
# ...You make me so lonely,
baby...#

261
00:15:36,770 --> 00:15:38,188
Lilo?

262
00:15:38,229 --> 00:15:40,065
We don't have time for this.

263
00:15:40,106 --> 00:15:41,399
# ...I get so lonely... #

264
00:15:41,441 --> 00:15:42,901
Leave me alone to die.

265
00:15:42,942 --> 00:15:44,319
Come on, Lilo

266
00:15:44,361 --> 00:15:46,404
that social worker's going
to be here any minute!

267
00:15:46,446 --> 00:15:47,739
# ...You still can find... #

268
00:15:47,781 --> 00:15:49,908
# ...some room... #

269
00:15:51,701 --> 00:15:55,372
# For brokenhearted lovers
to cry away their gloom #

270
00:15:57,791 --> 00:16:00,794
# Don't make me so lonely #

271
00:16:00,835 --> 00:16:02,671
# I get so lonely
I could die... #

272
00:16:05,882 --> 00:16:07,634
# The bellhop's tears
keep flowin'... #

273
00:16:07,676 --> 00:16:09,511
You are so finished
when I get in there!

274
00:16:09,552 --> 00:16:12,347
# Well, they been so long
on Lonely Street #

275
00:16:12,389 --> 00:16:14,891
# They ain't ever
gonna look back... #

276
00:16:14,933 --> 00:16:16,851
Oh, I'm going to stuff you
in the blender

277
00:16:16,893 --> 00:16:18,603
push "puree",
then bake you into a pie

278
00:16:18,645 --> 00:16:20,188
and feed it
to the social worker!

279
00:16:20,230 --> 00:16:21,940
And when he says,
"Mmm, this is great.

280
00:16:21,981 --> 00:16:23,942
What's your secret?"
I'm going to say...

281
00:16:24,984 --> 00:16:28,738
"Love... and nurturing."

282
00:16:28,780 --> 00:16:30,740
Hi. Uh...

283
00:16:32,283 --> 00:16:34,202
You must be the, uh...

284
00:16:34,244 --> 00:16:35,620
The stupidhead.

285
00:16:35,662 --> 00:16:37,622
Oh! Oh...

286
00:16:37,664 --> 00:16:39,833
Oh, you know,
I'm really sorry about that

287
00:16:39,874 --> 00:16:43,086
and if I'd known who you were,
of course I never would've...

288
00:16:43,128 --> 00:16:45,296
Uh... I can pay for that.

289
00:16:45,338 --> 00:16:46,631
It's a rental.

290
00:16:46,673 --> 00:16:48,675
Are you the guardian
in question?

291
00:16:48,717 --> 00:16:50,802
Yes. I'm Nani.

292
00:16:50,844 --> 00:16:52,887
Nice to meet you, Mister...?

293
00:16:52,929 --> 00:16:54,681
Bubbles.

294
00:16:54,723 --> 00:16:55,849
Mr. Bubbles.

295
00:16:55,890 --> 00:16:57,142
That's a strange...

296
00:16:57,183 --> 00:16:58,309
Yes, I know.

297
00:16:58,351 --> 00:17:01,021
Are you going
to invite me in, Nani?

298
00:17:01,062 --> 00:17:04,065
Uh... I thought we could
sit out here and talk.

299
00:17:04,107 --> 00:17:06,234
I don't think so.

300
00:17:06,276 --> 00:17:08,403
Right. Uh...

301
00:17:08,445 --> 00:17:10,572
# ...It's always crowded... #

302
00:17:10,613 --> 00:17:12,032
This way.

303
00:17:12,073 --> 00:17:13,908
# ...You still can find
some room #

304
00:17:14,034 --> 00:17:18,204
# For brokenhearted lovers
to cry away their gloom #

305
00:17:18,246 --> 00:17:21,249
# You make me so lonely,
baby... #

306
00:17:21,291 --> 00:17:24,461
Uh... wait here.

307
00:17:31,301 --> 00:17:32,385
Hey!

308
00:17:33,511 --> 00:17:34,971
So...

309
00:17:34,971 --> 00:17:37,140
lemonade?

310
00:17:37,182 --> 00:17:39,309
Do you often
leave your sister home alone?

311
00:17:39,351 --> 00:17:41,478
No. Never.

312
00:17:43,021 --> 00:17:44,647
Well, except forjust now.

313
00:17:44,689 --> 00:17:46,941
Uh, I had to run
to the store to get some...

314
00:17:49,027 --> 00:17:50,945
Oh!

315
00:17:50,987 --> 00:17:53,865
You left the stove on
while you were out?

316
00:17:53,907 --> 00:17:54,949
Low heat!

317
00:17:55,033 --> 00:17:55,992
Just a simmer.

318
00:17:56,034 --> 00:17:56,993
Mmm!

319
00:17:57,035 --> 00:17:58,203
It's coming along great.

320
00:18:00,330 --> 00:18:01,539
I found that this morning.

321
00:18:01,581 --> 00:18:03,124
Lilo! There you are.

322
00:18:03,166 --> 00:18:04,793
Honeyface...

323
00:18:04,834 --> 00:18:07,462
this is Mr. Bubbles.

324
00:18:07,504 --> 00:18:09,923
Nice to meet you.

325
00:18:10,006 --> 00:18:11,299
Your knuckles say "Cobra".

326
00:18:14,678 --> 00:18:17,472
Cobra Bubbles.

327
00:18:17,514 --> 00:18:20,183
You don't look like
a social worker.

328
00:18:20,225 --> 00:18:22,477
I'm a special classification.

329
00:18:22,519 --> 00:18:25,313
Did you ever kill anyone?

330
00:18:26,356 --> 00:18:28,525
We're getting off the subject.

331
00:18:28,566 --> 00:18:29,859
Let's talk about you.

332
00:18:29,901 --> 00:18:31,736
Are you happy?

333
00:18:34,447 --> 00:18:36,199
I'm adjusted.

334
00:18:36,241 --> 00:18:37,701
I eat four food groups

335
00:18:37,701 --> 00:18:40,620
and look both ways
before crossing the street

336
00:18:40,662 --> 00:18:43,206
and take long naps,
and get disciplined.

337
00:18:44,082 --> 00:18:45,083
Disciplined?

338
00:18:45,125 --> 00:18:48,169
Yeah.
She disciplines me real good.

339
00:18:48,211 --> 00:18:49,546
Sometimes five times a day.

340
00:18:49,587 --> 00:18:51,339
-With bricks.
-No...

341
00:18:51,381 --> 00:18:52,507
Bricks?

342
00:18:52,549 --> 00:18:54,175
Uh-huh, in a pillowcase.

343
00:18:54,217 --> 00:18:56,428
Okay! That's enough sugar
for you.

344
00:18:56,469 --> 00:18:59,305
Why don't you run along,
you little cutie.

345
00:19:00,473 --> 00:19:03,143
The other social workers
just thought she was a scream.

346
00:19:03,184 --> 00:19:04,144
Thirsty?

347
00:19:06,187 --> 00:19:09,858
Let me illuminate to you
the precarious situation

348
00:19:09,899 --> 00:19:12,444
in which you have
found yourself.

349
00:19:12,485 --> 00:19:17,615
I am the one they call
when things go wrong

350
00:19:17,657 --> 00:19:22,370
and things have
indeed gone wrong.

351
00:19:38,803 --> 00:19:41,556
My friends need to be punished.

352
00:19:45,435 --> 00:19:48,521
Call me next time
you're left here alone.

353
00:19:48,563 --> 00:19:50,648
Yep.

354
00:19:50,690 --> 00:19:53,651
In case you're wondering,
this did not go well.

355
00:19:55,653 --> 00:19:58,948
You have three days
to change my mind.

356
00:20:06,748 --> 00:20:08,500
-Blah.
-Eww!

357
00:20:08,541 --> 00:20:10,251
Lilo!

358
00:20:38,697 --> 00:20:40,407
Why didn't you wait
at the school?

359
00:20:40,448 --> 00:20:41,991
You were supposed
to wait there!

360
00:20:42,075 --> 00:20:43,368
Lilo!

361
00:20:43,410 --> 00:20:47,664
Do you not understand?
Do you want to be taken away?

362
00:20:47,706 --> 00:20:48,998
Answer me!

363
00:20:49,040 --> 00:20:50,000
No!

364
00:20:50,041 --> 00:20:51,334
No, you don't understand?

365
00:20:51,376 --> 00:20:52,377
No!

366
00:20:52,419 --> 00:20:53,378
No, what?

367
00:20:53,420 --> 00:20:55,005
No!

368
00:21:03,054 --> 00:21:04,347
You're such a pain!

369
00:21:04,389 --> 00:21:07,976
So why don't you sell me
and buy a rabbit instead?!

370
00:21:08,018 --> 00:21:11,271
At least a rabbit would behave
better than you!

371
00:21:11,312 --> 00:21:13,231
Go ahead!
Then you'll be happy

372
00:21:13,273 --> 00:21:15,692
because it'll be smarter
than me, too!

373
00:21:15,692 --> 00:21:17,193
And quieter!

374
00:21:17,235 --> 00:21:19,696
You'll like it,
'cause it's stinky, like you!

375
00:21:21,031 --> 00:21:22,991
Go to your room!

376
00:21:23,074 --> 00:21:24,993
I'm already in my room!

377
00:21:40,800 --> 00:21:42,093
Hey.

378
00:21:42,135 --> 00:21:47,557
I brought you some pizza,
in case you were hungry.

379
00:21:47,557 --> 00:21:50,852
We're a broken family,
aren't we?

380
00:21:50,894 --> 00:21:52,520
No.

381
00:21:54,564 --> 00:21:57,984
Maybe, a little.

382
00:21:58,109 --> 00:22:00,028
Maybe a lot.

383
00:22:00,111 --> 00:22:02,238
I shouldn't have yelled at you.

384
00:22:02,280 --> 00:22:05,742
We're sisters. It's our job.

385
00:22:05,742 --> 00:22:07,410
Yeah, well, from now on...

386
00:22:07,452 --> 00:22:10,413
I like you better as a sister
than a mom.

387
00:22:10,455 --> 00:22:13,208
Yeah?

388
00:22:13,249 --> 00:22:15,043
And you like me better
as a sister

389
00:22:15,085 --> 00:22:16,378
than a rabbit, right?

390
00:22:17,420 --> 00:22:18,713
Oh...

391
00:22:18,755 --> 00:22:20,423
Oh, oh, oh, oh.

392
00:22:21,758 --> 00:22:23,385
Yes.

393
00:22:23,426 --> 00:22:25,053
Yes, I do.

394
00:22:26,429 --> 00:22:28,723
I hit Mertle Edmonds today.

395
00:22:28,765 --> 00:22:30,058
You hit her?

396
00:22:30,100 --> 00:22:31,935
Before I bit her.

397
00:22:31,976 --> 00:22:33,478
You bit her.

398
00:22:33,520 --> 00:22:35,063
Lilo, you shouldn't...

399
00:22:35,105 --> 00:22:38,441
People treat me different.

400
00:22:38,483 --> 00:22:40,819
They just don't know
what to say.

401
00:22:40,860 --> 00:22:42,237
I'll tell you what.

402
00:22:42,278 --> 00:22:45,198
If you promise
not to fight anymore

403
00:22:45,240 --> 00:22:50,078
I promise not to yell at you,
except on special occasions.

404
00:22:50,120 --> 00:22:53,123
Tuesdays and bank
holidays would be good.

405
00:22:53,164 --> 00:22:54,457
Yeah? Would that be good?

406
00:22:55,834 --> 00:22:58,795
Oh! My camera's full again.

407
00:22:58,837 --> 00:23:01,506
Aren't they beautiful?

408
00:23:12,142 --> 00:23:13,435
A falling star!

409
00:23:18,314 --> 00:23:20,316
I call it! Get out! Get out!

410
00:23:20,358 --> 00:23:21,943
I have to make a wish!

411
00:23:22,027 --> 00:23:24,487
Can't you go any faster?

412
00:23:24,529 --> 00:23:27,240
Oh, no!
Gravity is increasing on me.

413
00:23:27,282 --> 00:23:28,450
No, it's not!

414
00:23:28,491 --> 00:23:29,492
It is, too, Lilo.

415
00:23:29,492 --> 00:23:31,119
The same thing
happened yesterday.

416
00:23:31,161 --> 00:23:35,123
You rotten sister!
Your butt is crushing me!

417
00:23:35,165 --> 00:23:36,958
Why do you act so weird?!

418
00:23:40,503 --> 00:23:42,797
It's me again.

419
00:23:42,839 --> 00:23:46,468
I need someone
to be my friend...

420
00:23:46,509 --> 00:23:49,637
someone who won't run away.

421
00:23:49,679 --> 00:23:52,474
Maybe send me an angel...

422
00:23:52,515 --> 00:23:55,643
the nicest angel you have.

423
00:24:41,231 --> 00:24:44,234
What we when hit?

424
00:24:46,611 --> 00:24:47,946
There it is.

425
00:24:47,987 --> 00:24:49,739
It stay jammed under the fender.

426
00:24:52,075 --> 00:24:53,910
We better call somebody.

427
00:25:11,469 --> 00:25:13,930
We're looking for something
that can defend itself...

428
00:25:13,972 --> 00:25:15,932
something that won't die...

429
00:25:16,057 --> 00:25:17,684
something sturdy, you know?

430
00:25:17,726 --> 00:25:18,893
Like a lobster.

431
00:25:18,935 --> 00:25:20,228
Lilo, you lolo.

432
00:25:20,270 --> 00:25:21,896
Do we have a lobster door?

433
00:25:21,938 --> 00:25:23,356
No. We have a dog door.

434
00:25:23,398 --> 00:25:24,733
We are getting a dog.

435
00:25:30,572 --> 00:25:33,783
So nice
to see your pretty face again!

436
00:25:33,825 --> 00:25:35,118
Jumba?

437
00:25:35,160 --> 00:25:37,746
We need your name and address
at the bottom of the form...

438
00:25:39,748 --> 00:25:42,292
The kennel's back this way.

439
00:25:42,334 --> 00:25:45,086
Go. Pick someone out.

440
00:25:47,005 --> 00:25:49,049
Hello?

441
00:25:51,051 --> 00:25:52,344
Hello?!

442
00:25:54,137 --> 00:25:57,140
Are there any "aminals" in here?

443
00:26:04,397 --> 00:26:05,940
Hello!

444
00:26:16,159 --> 00:26:17,118
Hi.

445
00:26:17,160 --> 00:26:19,120
Hoh... ha...

446
00:26:19,162 --> 00:26:21,081
Hi...

447
00:26:22,457 --> 00:26:23,833
Wow!

448
00:26:23,875 --> 00:26:24,959
Oh, yes. Mm-hmm.

449
00:26:25,001 --> 00:26:26,795
All of our dogs are adoptable.

450
00:26:26,836 --> 00:26:28,630
Except that one!

451
00:26:28,672 --> 00:26:30,632
What is that thing?!

452
00:26:30,674 --> 00:26:31,966
A dog, I think.

453
00:26:32,008 --> 00:26:33,510
But it was dead this morning.

454
00:26:33,551 --> 00:26:34,969
It was dead this morning?!

455
00:26:35,053 --> 00:26:37,972
Well, we thought it was dead.
It was hit by a truck.

456
00:26:38,014 --> 00:26:40,475
I like him!
Come here, boy.

457
00:26:42,727 --> 00:26:44,396
Oh! Aah!

458
00:26:45,689 --> 00:26:47,524
Wouldn't you like
a different dog?

459
00:26:47,565 --> 00:26:49,818
We have better dogs, dear.

460
00:26:49,859 --> 00:26:51,486
Not better than him.

461
00:26:51,528 --> 00:26:53,488
He can talk! Say hello.

462
00:26:53,530 --> 00:26:54,823
He... Hel...

463
00:26:54,864 --> 00:26:56,866
Dogs can't talk, dear.

464
00:26:56,908 --> 00:26:57,992
He did.

465
00:26:58,076 --> 00:27:00,829
Does it have to be this dog?

466
00:27:04,874 --> 00:27:06,167
Yes, he's good.

467
00:27:06,209 --> 00:27:07,419
I can tell.

468
00:27:07,460 --> 00:27:09,421
You'll have to think of a name
for him.

469
00:27:09,462 --> 00:27:12,590
His name is... Stitch.

470
00:27:12,632 --> 00:27:14,175
Now, that's not a real name...

471
00:27:14,217 --> 00:27:15,343
Hmm. Uh-uh, uh-uh-uh.

472
00:27:15,385 --> 00:27:18,680
...in Iceland...
but here, it's a good name.

473
00:27:18,722 --> 00:27:20,181
Stitch it is.

474
00:27:20,223 --> 00:27:21,933
And there's
a two dollar license fee.

475
00:27:22,058 --> 00:27:23,226
I want to buy him!

476
00:27:23,268 --> 00:27:25,979
Can I borrow two dollars?

477
00:27:31,568 --> 00:27:33,528
He's all yours.

478
00:27:33,570 --> 00:27:35,196
You're all mine.

479
00:27:35,238 --> 00:27:37,615
Well, what's he doing?

480
00:27:37,657 --> 00:27:39,159
Shh! Keep quiet.

481
00:27:39,200 --> 00:27:40,785
He's listening for us.

482
00:27:42,746 --> 00:27:45,206
How good is his hearing?

483
00:27:45,248 --> 00:27:46,541
I mean, can he...

484
00:27:53,173 --> 00:27:55,300
Why don't you run?

485
00:27:57,844 --> 00:27:59,304
Coming! I'm coming!

486
00:27:59,346 --> 00:28:00,680
Stop!

487
00:28:00,722 --> 00:28:02,849
I have just determined
this situation

488
00:28:02,891 --> 00:28:04,309
to be far too hazardous!

489
00:28:04,351 --> 00:28:06,519
Don't worry,
I won't hit her.

490
00:28:06,561 --> 00:28:10,482
No! That girl is a part
of the mosquito food chain.

491
00:28:10,523 --> 00:28:13,777
Here! Educate yourself.

492
00:28:13,818 --> 00:28:16,196
Using a little girl
for a shield.

493
00:28:16,237 --> 00:28:18,198
This is low, even for you!

494
00:28:18,239 --> 00:28:20,325
Whoo-hoo!

495
00:28:20,367 --> 00:28:21,368
Bah!

496
00:28:21,409 --> 00:28:24,245
Tear him apart
with all both my bare hands!

497
00:28:24,287 --> 00:28:25,372
Have you lost your mind?!

498
00:28:25,413 --> 00:28:26,790
What is it, Stitch?

499
00:28:26,831 --> 00:28:29,084
We cannot be seen!

500
00:28:30,794 --> 00:28:33,254
Bad dog, barking at nothing!

501
00:28:34,631 --> 00:28:37,258
You can't shoot,
and you can't be seen.

502
00:28:37,300 --> 00:28:38,426
Look at you!

503
00:28:38,468 --> 00:28:41,096
You look like a monster.

504
00:28:41,137 --> 00:28:42,472
We have to blend in.

505
00:28:42,681 --> 00:28:45,141
Okay, I got to get to work.

506
00:28:45,141 --> 00:28:47,644
Stick around town and stay
out of the roads, okay?

507
00:28:47,686 --> 00:28:48,853
I'll meet you at 1:00.

508
00:28:48,895 --> 00:28:50,689
Hmm?

509
00:28:50,730 --> 00:28:51,690
Oh!

510
00:28:51,731 --> 00:28:52,691
Ah!

511
00:28:57,821 --> 00:29:00,824
Okay, I guess
we should be going.

512
00:29:02,575 --> 00:29:04,577
What about Stitch?

513
00:29:11,167 --> 00:29:12,377
My friends!

514
00:29:16,464 --> 00:29:18,425
What do you want?

515
00:29:18,466 --> 00:29:19,801
I'm sorry I bit you

516
00:29:19,843 --> 00:29:21,344
and pulled your hair

517
00:29:21,344 --> 00:29:23,430
and punched you in the face.

518
00:29:23,471 --> 00:29:24,889
Apology not accepted.

519
00:29:24,931 --> 00:29:27,934
Now get out of my way
before I run you over.

520
00:29:29,310 --> 00:29:31,855
I got a new dog.
His name is Stitch.

521
00:29:31,896 --> 00:29:35,567
That is the ugliest thing
I have ever saw.

522
00:29:35,608 --> 00:29:37,819
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

523
00:29:37,861 --> 00:29:39,237
Eww! Get it away from me!

524
00:29:39,279 --> 00:29:40,655
I'm gonna get a disease!

525
00:29:45,744 --> 00:29:47,537
Somebody do something!

526
00:29:47,579 --> 00:29:48,955
Oh, great! He's loose.

527
00:29:48,997 --> 00:29:51,750
His destructive programming
is taking effect.

528
00:29:51,791 --> 00:29:54,544
He will be irresistibly
drawn to large cities

529
00:29:54,586 --> 00:29:56,338
where he will back up sewers

530
00:29:56,379 --> 00:29:59,674
reverse street signs and
steal everyone's left shoe.

531
00:30:18,026 --> 00:30:21,154
It's nice to live on an island
with no large cities.

532
00:30:25,033 --> 00:30:27,744
Are you okay?

533
00:30:31,915 --> 00:30:33,667
# Doo-doo #

534
00:30:33,708 --> 00:30:35,001
# Doo-doo #

535
00:30:35,043 --> 00:30:38,380
# You can shake an apple
off an apple tree #

536
00:30:38,421 --> 00:30:42,300
# Shake-a, shake-a, sugar,
but you'll never shake me #

537
00:30:42,342 --> 00:30:44,010
-# Uh-uh-uh #
-# Doo-doo-doo #

538
00:30:44,094 --> 00:30:45,929
# No, siree, uh-uh... #

539
00:30:45,970 --> 00:30:47,222
Uh-uh.

540
00:30:47,263 --> 00:30:48,515
# ...Doo-doo-doo #

541
00:30:48,556 --> 00:30:50,392
